[calm, slow] Just because they're family
doesn't mean they'll *show* up when it matters.

[soft] This is hard because you keep making excuses for them.
Maybe they were busy.
Maybe they didn't know how bad it was.
Maybe next time will be different.
And part of you still believes
you asked for too *much*.

[sad] But you remember.
The surgery they couldn't make it to.
The funeral where you kept looking for their face.
The night you needed help, (pause) and they had other plans.


[firm] That's not a small thing. That's an *answer*.
Love isn't only what people say.
It's where they are when your life falls apart.

You stopped asking.
Not because you stopped caring.
Because you got *tired*
of being the only one who did.

They didn't lose you all at once.
They lost you one empty chair at a time.

[soft] Some people are family by blood.
Some are family by showing up.
[intense, slow] (long pause) You're allowed to know the *difference*.


[soft, slow] Keep your heart for the people
who come when you (pause) call.
